    "The query is a prodrug ester; parent F may be low while active metabolite exposure could differ, and this distinction is not resolved.",
    "L3 oral exposure records lack IV comparators, so they do not directly quantify absolute F.",
    "L4 permeability/solubility records are in vitro and for other steroids, not the query; high permeability and low solubility leave the absorption component partially unresolved.",
    "Transfer from steroid/terpenoid and prodrug contexts is structural/mechanistic analogy, not an exact match."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low (F<20%) because the query is a lipophilic, poorly soluble neutral corticosteroid acetal ester prodrug, and the most transferable human-relevant contexts (AKBA, withaferin A, estradiol, β-sitosterol, paclitaxel, perindoprilat, cyclandelate) all show measured oral bioavailability below 20%. L3 oral exposure records for fluticasone propionate and beclomethasone dipropionate show very low plasma Cmax/AUC after oral dosing, further supporting low oral systemic exposure for this corticosteroid prodrug class. L4 steroid solubility data are consistent with solubility-limited absorption, while high permeability data do not overcome the first-pass and low-exposure evidence; L2 high values are species-specific or unverified and do not overturn the low direction."
}

